From 02599dfa5bff307d14ac943a7b53b8d085b05c51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 05:31:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 17/33] feat: Hybrid DOF 2.0 two-domain mask, effect authority,
 camera slots + tracker follow

Renderer (DepthOfField / PostProcess):
- Two-domain aperture model: hard crossover at Mask Aperture; mask domain uses the
  texture silhouette (contour ring), iris domain the polygon. Blade Curvature as a
  polygon sharpening exponent shared by gather taps and splat mask.
- Full-res source sampling with per-texel excess (fixes 16x luminance dilution), dedicated
  full-res splat layers, r_DepthOfFieldResolutionScale grid tiers, mask transmittance
  compensation, unified splat energy rule.
- Gather importance sampling from the mask DDS (CryPak read -> 2D CDF); Hammersley tap
  set instead of the regular grid (regular grid collapsed to 7 mask rows under CDF
  inversion -> note fragments); one-shot domain transition logs.
- Stock bug fixes: CParamTexture::SyncMainWithRender never propagated main->render and
  never cleared the render-side flag (one Reset overrode the texture forever); user focus
  branch no longer double-smoothed on the render thread.
- cvar naming unified to r_DepthOfField* (BokehShapeStrength, SpriteBokehDebug,
  ResolutionScale); internal CV_r_Dof* names kept per engine precedent.

CinematicCamera plugin:
- Single ownership authority: the camera manager decides the active camera, s_pActive is
  a per-frame resolved cache; dethroned cameras hand the render state back. Every Apply*
  gated on ownership and Preview mode. RESET handled bidirectionally (enter = drop stale
  baselines, leave = restore). Dof_Active / ApertureBlades / FNumber now saved+restored.
- Edit-mode policy made uniform: view-dependent effects game-mode only.
- Preview camera component flagged NoSave + duplicate purge (one extra camera per
  save/load cycle before).
- Camera Slot (1-9) + ccam_slot console command; C exports for active-camera entity and
  slot activation.

CryPhoneTracker plugin:
- Follow Active Camera: the controller drives whichever cinematic camera is active,
  re-anchoring on every switch and re-sending lens state; falls back to its own entity.
- Tracker ID, port-conflict diagnostics, stacked per-tracker debug overlay with peer IP
  and driven target.

Docs: READMEs and ConsoleReference rewritten from source (English); EffectAuthoritySpec
added. RenderDoc-measured cost of the full feature set: ~0.09 ms GPU per frame.

