@@ -1,160 +1,259 @@
 # CryPhoneTracker
 
-CRYENGINE 5.7 原生 plugin，提供 **Phone Tracker** entity component（Sandbox 分類：**Tracking / Phone Tracker**）：接收 Android ARCore 手機追蹤器（`cryengine-57-lts/androidtracker`）送出的封包，用 6DoF pose 驅動 entity 的位置與旋轉，並把手機上的鏡頭推桿（focal length / aperture / focus / ISO / EV）轉交給同一個 entity 上的 **Cinematic Camera** component。
-
-## 連線
-
-- Component 在進入 game mode／simulation 時開一個 **UDP** socket（`Listen Port`，預設 9050），非阻塞、每幀把 socket 讀空，entity 永遠追最新的 pose 而不是積壓的舊值。純編輯模式下 entity 收不到 Update 事件，不會動——這是引擎行為。
-- 手機 App 的 Settings 填 PC 的區網 IP 與相同 Port，Transport 選 UDP。
-- 控制封包（Recenter、AF 結果等）從同一個 socket 回送到最後收到封包的手機位址。
-
-## 座標與 Transform Mapping
-
-ARCore 與 CRYENGINE 同為右手座標系，只需換軸：位置 `(x, y, z)` → `(x, −z, y)`，四元數 `(qx, qy, qz, qw)` → `(qx, −qz, qy, qw)`（與 `tools/pose_monitor.py` 一致）。
-
-Pose 管線順序：**PoseFilter（tracker 空間，公尺）→ MapToWorld（原點／yaw／縮放／偏移）→ 選配的 legacy smoothing → 寫入 entity**。閾值全部在物理單位上運作，不受 `Metres To Units` 影響。
-
-**Align Yaw On Start**（預設開）：錨定時只取「起始 pose 的 yaw」（手機端與 entity 端皆然），pitch 與 roll 維持重力對齊——轉手機永遠繞世界 Z 軸轉 entity。關閉時若拍攝開始瞬間手機是斜的，整個旋轉座標系都會跟著斜。手機朝上／朝下看時 yaw 改由 up 軸推導，不會退化。
-
-Recenter（Schematyc 函式或手機端自行 recenter，`originEpoch` 遞增時自動跟上）會把**濾波後**的 pose 當新原點（抖動不會凍進原點），並把當下 entity transform 重新當參考點，所以 recenter 不會讓 entity 瞬移。
-
-## PoseFilter 管線
-
-`Module/PoseFilter.h`，header-only、無 gEnv、無動態配置，可在引擎外單元測試。四個階段：
-
-| 階段 | 執行時機 | 內容 |
+A native CRYENGINE 5.7 plugin providing the **Phone Tracker** entity component (Sandbox
+category: **Tracking / Phone Tracker**): it receives packets from the Android ARCore phone
+tracker (`cryengine-57-lts/androidtracker`), drives an entity's position and rotation from the
+6DoF pose, and forwards the lens faders on the phone (focal length / aperture / focus / ISO /
+EV) to a **Cinematic Camera** component.
+
+## Connection
+
+- The component opens a **UDP** socket when entering game/simulation mode (`Listen Port`,
+  default 9050), non-blocking, drained empty every frame, so the entity always follows the
+  newest pose instead of a backlog. In pure edit mode the entity receives no Update event and
+  does not move — that is engine behaviour.
+- In the phone app's Settings, enter the PC's LAN IP and the same port, transport UDP.
+- Control packets (Recenter, AF results) are sent back through the same socket to the address
+  the last packet came from.
+- **Port conflicts are named.** Two trackers on one port would silently fight over the bind
+  (and the loser would get no packets and no error), so before binding, the component looks
+  for another live tracker on the same port and refuses with
+  `PORT 9050 BUSY - held by tracker #2 'CamRig'` — shown both as a warning in the log and in
+  the debug overlay. A port taken outside the level reports
+  `PORT 9050 BIND FAILED - in use outside this level (another process?)`.
+
+### Tracker ID
+
+**Tracker ID** (Connection group, 0-99, default 0) is the number this tracker answers to in
+logs and in the debug overlay, so several trackers can be told apart. `0` means automatic:
+the tracker's position in creation order, 1-based. Every log line and the overlay carry it
+(`[PhoneTracker] #1 'PhoneCam': listening for pose packets on UDP port 9050`).
+
+## Following the active cinematic camera
+
+**Follow Active Camera** (Transform Mapping, default on) makes the tracker drive whichever
+Cinematic Camera is currently active instead of its own entity — so the phone becomes the
+operator of whatever camera the console command `ccam_slot N` (or a Schematyc `Activate`)
+selected. The active camera entity is resolved through the C entry point
+`CryGetActiveCinematicCameraEntity()` exported by `CinematicCamera.dll`.
+
+On every switch:
+
+- The tracker **re-anchors** on the new camera: its reference transform is re-captured from
+  where that camera was placed, and the next pose re-captures the tracker origin against it
+  (the recenter path), so the phone carries on from wherever the new camera sits instead of
+  teleporting it. The phone's own frame is left alone — no control packet is sent.
+- The pose filter is reset, so no transient from the previous camera carries over.
+- The **lens link follows too**: the new camera's optics are resolved and immediately handed
+  the lens state the phone last sent, so the cut does not land on stale lens values.
+- The switch is logged: `[PhoneTracker] #1 'PhoneCam': controller now drives 'CamB'`.
+
+When no cinematic camera is active (or the CinematicCamera plugin is not loaded), the tracker
+falls back to driving its own entity.
+
+## Coordinates and Transform Mapping
+
+ARCore and CRYENGINE are both right handed, so only an axis swap is needed: position
+`(x, y, z)` -> `(x, -z, y)`, quaternion `(qx, qy, qz, qw)` -> `(qx, -qz, qy, qw)` (matching
+`tools/pose_monitor.py`).
+
+Pose pipeline order: **PoseFilter (tracker space, metres) -> MapToWorld (origin / yaw / scale /
+offset) -> optional legacy smoothing -> written to the entity**. All thresholds operate in
+physical units and are unaffected by `Metres To Units`.
+
+**Align Yaw On Start** (default on): anchoring uses only the yaw of the starting poses (phone
+and entity alike); pitch and roll stay gravity aligned, so turning the phone always rotates the
+entity around the world up axis. With it off, a phone tilted at capture time tilts the whole
+rotation frame. With the phone looking straight up or down the heading is taken from the up
+axis instead, so it never degenerates.
+
+Recenter (the Schematyc function, or the phone recentering itself — the incrementing
+`originEpoch` is followed automatically) takes the **filtered** pose as the new origin (so
+jitter is never frozen into it) and re-captures the current target transform as the reference,
+so recentering never teleports the entity.
+
+## PoseFilter pipeline
+
+`Module/PoseFilter.h`, header-only, no `gEnv`, no dynamic allocation, unit-testable outside the
+engine. Four stages:
+
+| Stage | Runs | Contents |
 | --- | --- | --- |
-| A 時鐘重定 | 每個封包 | 把手機 frame timestamp 映射到引擎時鐘：EMA 吸收漂移（每包最多修正 2 ms），偏差超過 200 ms 視為手機時鐘跳變、整組重置。 |
-| B One Euro | 每個封包 | 位置三軸共用 cutoff（`posMinCutoff + posBeta × 速度`）、旋轉走最短弧＋角速率自適應。 |
-| B' 固定延遲重取樣 | 每個渲染幀 | 16 格 ring buffer，在引擎時鐘後方 `封包間隔 × Resample Delay` 處取樣：位置用濾波速度作切線的 cubic Hermite、旋轉 slerp。訊號中斷時最多外插 `Max Extrapolation` 毫秒（速度線性衰減），之後凍結在最後 pose，永不回彈。 |
-| C 虛擬腳架 | 每個渲染幀 | 見下節，只有 Cinematic 模式啟用。 |
+| A clock rebasing | per packet | Maps phone frame timestamps onto the engine clock: an EMA absorbs drift (at most 2 ms correction per packet); a deviation over 200 ms is treated as a phone clock jump and resets the set. |
+| B One Euro | per packet | Position uses one cutoff for all three axes (`posMinCutoff + posBeta * speed`); rotation takes the shortest arc with an angular-rate adaptive cutoff. |
+| B' fixed delay resampling | per render frame | 16-slot ring buffer sampled `packet interval * Resample Delay` behind the engine clock: cubic Hermite for position (tangents from the filtered velocity), slerp for rotation. During a signal gap the pose is extrapolated for at most `Max Extrapolation` ms (velocity decaying linearly), then frozen on the last pose — never snapping back. |
+| C virtual tripod | per render frame | See below; Cinematic mode only. |
 
